WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.387
This feature looks

00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:02.413
useless until it

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.121
costs you

00:00:03.654 --> 00:00:04.656
In a simulated

00:00:04.468 --> 00:00:06.024
table of 40,000

00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:06.826
ride requests

00:00:07.038 --> 00:00:08.087
removing the city

00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:08.960
column drops the

00:00:08.772 --> 00:00:10.328
model's AUC by

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.979
0.169

00:00:12.274 --> 00:00:13.123
yet alone it

00:00:12.935 --> 00:00:14.373
scores like noise

00:00:14.902 --> 00:00:16.175
Price alone scores

00:00:15.987 --> 00:00:17.755
0.693

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.887
but price plus

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:21.222
city reaches 0.860

00:00:21.459 --> 00:00:22.484
within a whisker

00:00:22.296 --> 00:00:23.109
of the best

00:00:22.921 --> 00:00:25.149
possible 0.861

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:26.436
In a pool

00:00:26.248 --> 00:00:28.335
of 196 columns

00:00:28.288 --> 00:00:29.549
four useful features

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:30.328
were invisible to

00:00:30.139 --> 00:00:31.318
univariate tests

00:00:31.507 --> 00:00:32.108
so use a

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.594
boosted model's loss-based

00:00:33.406 --> 00:00:34.644
importance instead

00:00:35.166 --> 00:00:36.180
Full story on

00:00:35.991 --> 00:00:36.887
the dashboard
